       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Dose:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg per dose is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** Four doses a day comes to 6,400 mg/day. The maximum for adults in a hospital is 3,200 mg/day, and that is for the short term. A total of 6,400 mg raises the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1,600 mg/day)\n- 600 mg by mouth four times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2,400 mg/day)\n- 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- 1,600 mg total per day, split into smaller doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. A note with the clinical rationale would also help."
